            },
            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The change tightens the approval digest: it now covers the owner execute bit and refuses names with a backslash. Both make approvals harder to bypass, not easier.",
              "skillsfs/approvals.go reads bytes and mode from a single no-follow descriptor and reports a swapped symlink or non-regular file as its real type, so the domain refuses it. This closes a race instead of opening one. A pipe cannot block the read.",
              "The new test in engine/skills/registry_lock_e2e_test.go requires validate on the real tree to exit 0, so a stale committed approval now fails the test rather than being tolerated.",
              "The version 2 records are digest metadata only. I found no secrets, no unsafe input handling and no dependency changes. The documented recompute recipe quotes its variables and uses a find -perm check with no injection path.",
              "No exploitable defect that this candidate introduced was found."
            ]
          }
        }
